1
00:00:06,430 --> 00:00:09,120
A 5 metre ladder leans against a wall.

2
00:00:09,170 --> 00:00:11,790
Its foot is 1.4 metres from the wall.

3
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:15,440
The wall and the ground make a right angle.

4
00:00:15,490 --> 00:00:18,360
How high up the wall does the ladder reach?

5
00:00:18,410 --> 00:00:21,930
Pause the video and work it out.

6
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:26,340
Height squared is 5 squared minus 1.4 squared.

7
00:00:26,390 --> 00:00:29,980
That is 25 minus 1.96, which is 23.04.

8
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:34,260
The square root of 23.04 is 4.8 metres.

9
00:00:34,310 --> 00:00:36,970
This uses Pythagoras' theorem.

10
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:42,520
Remember: 6 squared is 36, and the square root of 49 is 7.

11
00:00:42,570 --> 00:00:46,900
In a right-angled triangle, the longest side is the hypotenuse, C.

12
00:00:46,950 --> 00:00:49,370
Call the other sides A and B.

13
00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:54,930
Pythagoras' theorem says: A squared plus B squared equals C squared.

14
00:00:54,980 --> 00:00:58,670
Check with 3, 4 and 5: 9 plus 16 is 25.

15
00:00:58,720 --> 00:00:59,350
Your turn.

16
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:04,650
Where is the hypotenuse: opposite the right angle, or is it the shortest side?

17
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:07,880
Pause the video and choose.

18
00:01:07,930 --> 00:01:10,890
The hypotenuse is opposite the right angle.

19
00:01:10,940 --> 00:01:13,530
It is always the longest side.

20
00:01:13,580 --> 00:01:19,370
To find a shorter side, rearrange: A squared equals C squared minus B squared.

21
00:01:19,420 --> 00:01:20,710
Here is the method.

22
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:25,720
Step 1: find the hypotenuse: the side opposite the right angle.

23
00:01:25,770 --> 00:01:28,810
Step 2: square the sides you know.

24
00:01:28,860 --> 00:01:31,100
Step 3: for the hypotenuse, add.

25
00:01:31,150 --> 00:01:33,740
For a shorter side, subtract.

26
00:01:33,790 --> 00:01:39,210
Step 4: take the square root, and check the hypotenuse is the longest.

27
00:01:39,260 --> 00:01:44,670
A right-angled triangle has sides of 5 and 12 centimetres.

28
00:01:44,720 --> 00:01:46,460
25 plus 144 is 169.

29
00:01:46,510 --> 00:01:50,860
The square root of 169 is 13 centimetres.

30
00:01:50,910 --> 00:01:51,620
Your turn.

31
00:01:51,670 --> 00:01:54,270
The two shorter sides are 9 and 12.

32
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:55,790
Find the hypotenuse.

33
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:58,860
Pause and work it out.

34
00:01:58,910 --> 00:02:01,110
81 plus 144 is 225.

35
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:05,100
The square root of 225 is 15.

36
00:02:05,150 --> 00:02:09,950
The hypotenuse is 17 metres, and one side is 8 metres.

37
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,640
Subtract: 289 minus 64 is 225.

38
00:02:12,690 --> 00:02:15,790
The square root is 15 metres.

39
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:20,580
The hypotenuse is 13 centimetres, and one side is 5 centimetres.

40
00:02:20,630 --> 00:02:22,520
Lily finds the other side.

41
00:02:22,570 --> 00:02:24,560
Which line is wrong?

42
00:02:24,610 --> 00:02:25,690
Line 1 is wrong.

43
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:27,730
For a shorter side, subtract.

44
00:02:27,780 --> 00:02:32,640
Her answer is longer than the hypotenuse, which is impossible.

45
00:02:32,690 --> 00:02:34,740
169 minus 25 is 144.

46
00:02:34,790 --> 00:02:38,870
The square root is 12 centimetres.

47
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:40,920
Builders use the 3 4 5 rule.

48
00:02:40,970 --> 00:02:50,400
If a corner has sides of 3 metres and 4 metres, and the diagonal is exactly 5 metres, the corner is a perfect right angle.

49
00:02:50,450 --> 00:02:51,730
One last question.

50
00:02:51,780 --> 00:02:55,360
Is a triangle with sides 5, 6 and 8 right-angled?

51
00:02:55,410 --> 00:02:58,760
Pause the video and choose.

52
00:02:58,810 --> 00:03:00,250
25 plus 36 is 61.

53
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:02,000
But 8 squared is 64.

54
00:03:02,050 --> 00:03:06,580
They are not equal, so it is not right-angled.

55
00:03:06,630 --> 00:03:12,780
To remember: A squared plus B squared equals C squared, where C is the hypotenuse.

56
00:03:12,830 --> 00:03:14,440
For the hypotenuse, add.

57
00:03:14,490 --> 00:03:17,000
For a shorter side, subtract.

58
00:03:17,050 --> 00:03:19,950
The hypotenuse is the longest side.

59
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:25,590
If A squared plus B squared equals C squared, the angle is 90 degrees.

60
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:30,830
Great work! Now practise lesson 5.5 on Camday.
